# Postmortem: unmerged caller integration test records

The integration-testing entry point retained "current" records for two revisions at the same time. The first thing noticed was that the public API regression did not match the old record; looking back from the entry point, both appeared to be the current version, so the page labels alone could not establish which one had been adopted first.

The original input and the entry-point version were saved at the time, and the same request was not repeatedly resubmitted for integration testing. This was to prevent a new result from overwriting discrepancies already present in the old record. The client request context could later be recovered, but that does not mean the relationship between the two revisions has been clarified.

The initial suspicion was that the difference was confined to the V2 Core namespace migration. That suspicion was not confirmed; it is being retained as an investigative starting point, not as a basis for recovery. What can be confirmed at this point is that the user path deviated and was later restored; the time of recovery is distinct from the time of cause confirmation.

Still missing:

- The order in which the two revisions were added to the entry point;
- The last confirmable state before the failure;
- Which callers actually used one of the records;
- Whether the V2 Core namespace change was related to this deviation.

DOC-33 contains the migration index for the old entry point; no migration steps are added here. On subsequent review, first confirm which entry-point record is open before discussing the path after recovery.
